{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be helping take care of you during your stay. You came in with worsening abdominal pain and vomiting—can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. The pain has been getting worse over the past week. It’s in my upper left and right belly, near my G tube. My usual morphine suppositories aren’t helping at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned vomiting every day for the last few days?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, daily for about a week now. Phenergan isn’t touching the nausea. I haven’t slept well because of the pain and vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds really tough. We’ve reviewed your imaging—an X-ray showed some air-fluid levels, but no sign of a complete blockage. The surgical team doesn’t think you need surgery right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not another bowel obstruction?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not a complete one. It could be a partial slowdown, which fits with your history of sclerosing mesenteritis. We’ll manage your pain and nausea while keeping you on your TPN through your femoral line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My G tube output has also gone way up—1200 to 2200 cc a day. It used to be around 300."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s consistent with increased gut activity or irritation. We’ll keep monitoring it. For now, we’re going to keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—so your gut can rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s fine. But please, I need better pain control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We’re starting IV Dilaudid every 4 hours and IV Phenergan every 6 hours. We’ll watch how you respond and adjust as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve been so frustrated. This pain is constant and nothing’s working like it used to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. It’s a lot to manage. We’ve asked social work to check in with you—they can help with emotional support and coping strategies."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-10-28 02:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d appreciate that. Sometimes the emotional pain feels just as bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-10-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain now after the first round of IV meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-10-28 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better, maybe down to a 7 from a 10. But it’s still really uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-10-28 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep the IV pain meds going and reassess. Your labs are stable—no signs of infection or kidney issues. We’ll continue TPN through your femoral line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-10-28 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is my line okay? I’ve had problems with it before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-10-28 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked it. There’s tenderness near the site, but no infection. However, the external part of the catheter looks worn. We may need to replace it later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-10-28 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Again? It’s split before in the same spot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-10-28 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re aware. It’s likely due to movement and positioning. We’ll plan for a replacement when you’re more stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-10-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today we’re scheduled to replace your G tube. It was already due, and we think it’s a good time to do it while you’re here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-10-30 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it safe? I’m worried about more pain afterward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-10-30 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a routine procedure. We’ll use local numbing gel. Most patients tolerate it well. We’ll give extra pain meds just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-10-30 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The G tube was replaced successfully. The old one was removed and a new one placed over a guidewire. The site looks clean."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-10-30 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt some pressure, but not too bad. How’s the output now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-10-30 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still high, but we’ll keep monitoring. We’re starting to transition you back to rectal morphine and Phenergan since you’re tolerating things better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-10-30 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can we increase the morphine? 20 mg isn’t cutting it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-10-30 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re increasing it to 25 mg every 6 hours as needed. We’ll watch for side effects like drowsiness or slow breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-11-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing better. Pain is down, and you’re off IV meds. We’re keeping you on TPN and your new G tube is working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-11-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. But I’m still anxious about the femoral line. When will it be replaced?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-11-01 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re scheduling it for early next week. It’s important to fix it before it fails completely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-11-02 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pain is now at a 3-4 with the 25 mg morphine. That’s a big improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-11-02 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, finally something is helping. I’ve even slept a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-11-02 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll keep you on the current plan. Social work stopped by—they said you had a good talk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-11-02 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it helped. I’m still overwhelmed, but I feel heard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-11-04 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning your discharge later this week. First, we’ll replace your femoral line tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-11-04 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous. Will it be done under sedation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-11-04 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll get light sedation—fentanyl and Versed—so you’ll be relaxed and won’t feel much. It’s a quick procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-11-04 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that helps. And my other meds will stay the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-11-04 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mostly. The only change is the morphine dose—now 25 mg PR every 6 hours as needed. Everything else continues as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-11-06 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You just had your femoral line replaced. It went smoothly—you tolerated it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-11-06 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t even remember much. Is it secure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-11-06 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, new catheter is in place, cuff positioned correctly. You can use it right away for TPN and meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Now that the line is fixed and your pain is controlled, we’re ready to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your gastroenterologist and pain clinic as scheduled. And please follow up with your psychiatrist—we think that’s important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve realized how much the emotional side affects my pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Managing both is key. At home, keep using the 25 mg morphine PR as needed, but hold it if you’re drowsy or breathing slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my G tube and line care?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same as before—flush the G tube regularly, care for the skin, and do the ethanol lock for the line daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can manage that. Thank you for listening and adjusting my pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We know this is a chronic struggle. We’re here to support you through each flare-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It means a lot. I’ll keep in touch with my team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You should be home within a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready. It’s good to be going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure you have all your prescriptions updated, especially the new morphine dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. I don’t want to run out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’ll be filled before you leave. And if pain worsens, don’t hesitate to call your doctor or come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll stay in touch. I’ve learned to speak up when things aren’t working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best thing you can do. Keep advocating for yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for respecting that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. That’s how we get the best outcomes—together."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel hopeful. That’s a good place to be."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad to hear that. Rest up at home and take it one day at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for the support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll make sure your home health nurse is set up to help with your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve already spoken to them. It’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We want you to feel supported at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do. I’m ready to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get the discharge order processed. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2184-11-06 10:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll follow up with all my doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care of yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you soon, hopefully not in the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hope so too. But we’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s comforting to know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Always. Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take it easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ll be there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2184-11-06 11:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re rooting for you."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-10-28 01:41:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-11-06 14:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of sclerosing mesenteritis, recurrent small bowel obstructions, and chronic TPN via a femoral catheter was admitted for worsening abdominal pain and persistent vomiting. Imaging showed no complete bowel obstruction, and the surgical team recommended medical management. She was initially NPO and treated with IV Dilaudid and Phenergan for pain and nausea. Her G tube was replaced as scheduled, and her morphine dose was increased to 25 mg PR every 6 hours due to inadequate pain control. A mechanical complication of her femoral central venous line—repeated splitting of the external portion—led to its replacement. She was transitioned back to home medications, including rectal morphine and Phenergan, with improved symptom control. Social work supported her emotional distress, which was multifactorial. She was discharged home with updated pain management, follow-up plans with gastroenterology, pain clinic, and mental health providers, and no pending studies.",
    "problems": [
      "Abdominal pain, generalized",
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Malnutrition of moderate degree",
      "Chronic venous embolism and thrombosis of unspecified deep vessels of lower extremity",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Attention to gastrostomy",
      "Mechanical complication of other vascular device, implant, and graft",
      "Chronic hepatitis C without mention of hepatic coma",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Myoclonus",
      "Dehydration",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Persistent vomiting",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus"
    ]
  }
}
